## 5. Data

```yaml id=DATA kind=data
entities:
  - id: ENT-Employee
    name: Employee
    plain_name: People
    fields:
      - name: name
      - name: email
      - name: phone
        required: false
      - name: job_title
      - name: department
      - name: photo
        type: image
        required: false
      - name: manager
        type: ref
        required: false
        ref: ENT-Employee
      - name: location
        required: false
        description: Site or office
      - name: is_active
        type: bool
      - name: location_consent
        type: bool
        required: false
        description: Whether the person agreed to share exact location
    seed_guidance: 12 to 20 employees across three or four departments, one manager per department, with
      believable job titles and sites.
  - id: ENT-Task
    name: Task
    plain_name: Tasks
    fields:
      - name: title
      - name: description
        type: text
        required: false
      - name: status
        type: enum
        enum: TaskStatus
      - name: priority
        type: enum
        enum: Priority
      - name: due_at
        type: datetime
        required: false
      - name: assignee
        type: ref
        required: false
        ref: ENT-Employee
      - name: created_by
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-Employee
      - name: location
        required: false
      - name: form_template
        type: ref
        required: false
        ref: ENT-FormTemplate
        description: Checklist or form to complete for this task
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [todo, in_progress, blocked, done]
      transitions:
        - {from: todo, target: in_progress, 'on': start}
        - {from: in_progress, target: blocked, 'on': block}
        - {from: blocked, target: in_progress, 'on': unblock}
        - {from: in_progress, target: done, 'on': complete}
    seed_guidance: 10 to 15 tasks for the main employee, due today, tomorrow and overdue, a few with a
      checklist attached.
  - id: ENT-TaskComment
    name: Task comment
    plain_name: Task comments
    fields:
      - {name: task, type: ref, ref: ENT-Task}
      - {name: author, type: ref, ref: ENT-Employee}
      - {name: body, type: text}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
  - id: ENT-FormTemplate
    name: Form template
    plain_name: Forms and checklists
    fields:
      - name: name
      - name: description
        type: text
        required: false
      - name: kind
        type: enum
        enum: FormKind
      - name: fields
        type: json
        description: 'Field or checklist item definitions: label, type, required'
      - name: requires_photo
        type: bool
      - name: estimated_minutes
        type: int
        required: false
    seed_guidance: Five templates such as a site safety checklist, a vehicle check, an incident report,
      a delivery sign-off and a visit report.
  - id: ENT-FormSubmission
    name: Form submission
    plain_name: Submitted forms
    fields:
      - {name: template, type: ref, ref: ENT-FormTemplate}
      - {name: submitted_by, type: ref, ref: ENT-Employee}
      - {name: task, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-Task}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: SubmissionStatus}
      - {name: answers, type: json}
      - {name: photos, type: json, required: false, description: List of uploaded photo references}
      - {name: submitted_at, type: datetime, required: false}
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [draft, submitted]
      transitions:
        - {from: draft, target: submitted, 'on': submit}
  - id: ENT-ApprovalRequest
    name: Approval request
    plain_name: Requests
    fields:
      - {name: kind, type: enum, enum: RequestKind}
      - {name: title}
      - {name: details, type: text, required: false}
      - {name: requester, type: ref, ref: ENT-Employee}
      - {name: approver, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-Employee}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: ApprovalStatus}
      - {name: amount, type: money, required: false}
      - {name: starts_on, type: date, required: false}
      - {name: ends_on, type: date, required: false}
      - {name: decision_note, required: false}
      - {name: decided_at, type: datetime, required: false}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [pending, approved, rejected, withdrawn]
      transitions:
        - {from: pending, target: approved, 'on': approve}
        - {from: pending, target: rejected, 'on': reject}
        - {from: pending, target: withdrawn, 'on': withdraw}
    seed_guidance: Five requests across kinds and statuses, three waiting for the sample manager.
  - id: ENT-Timesheet
    name: Timesheet
    plain_name: Timesheets
    fields:
      - {name: employee, type: ref, ref: ENT-Employee}
      - {name: week_start, type: date}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: TimesheetStatus}
      - {name: total_minutes, type: int}
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [open, submitted, approved, rejected]
      transitions:
        - {from: open, target: submitted, 'on': submit}
        - {from: submitted, target: approved, 'on': approve}
        - {from: submitted, target: rejected, 'on': reject}
        - {from: rejected, target: open, 'on': reopen}
  - id: ENT-TimeEntry
    name: Time entry
    plain_name: Time entries
    fields:
      - {name: timesheet, type: ref, ref: ENT-Timesheet}
      - {name: work_date, type: date}
      - {name: minutes, type: int, description: 'Whole minutes, never fractional hours'}
      - {name: task, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-Task}
      - {name: project, required: false}
      - {name: note, required: false}
  - id: ENT-Announcement
    name: Announcement
    plain_name: Announcements
    fields:
      - {name: title}
      - {name: body, type: text}
      - {name: author, type: ref, ref: ENT-Employee}
      - {name: published_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: pinned, type: bool}
      - {name: requires_ack, type: bool}
    source: research
  - id: ENT-AnnouncementAck
    name: Announcement acknowledgement
    plain_name: Read confirmations
    fields:
      - {name: announcement, type: ref, ref: ENT-Announcement}
      - {name: employee, type: ref, ref: ENT-Employee}
      - {name: acknowledged_at, type: datetime}
    source: research
  - id: ENT-SyncItem
    name: Sync item
    plain_name: Changes waiting to sync
    fields:
      - {name: label, description: 'For example Safety checklist, Site 4'}
      - {name: entity_type}
      - {name: state, type: enum, enum: SyncState}
      - {name: queued_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: error, required: false}
    source: research
enums:
  - {name: TaskStatus, values: [todo, in_progress, blocked, done]}
  - {name: Priority, values: [low, normal, high, urgent]}
  - {name: FormKind, values: [form, checklist]}
  - {name: SubmissionStatus, values: [draft, submitted]}
  - {name: RequestKind, values: [leave, expense, equipment, other]}
  - {name: ApprovalStatus, values: [pending, approved, rejected, withdrawn]}
  - {name: TimesheetStatus, values: [open, submitted, approved, rejected]}
  - {name: SyncState, values: [pending, failed, conflict]}
seed_guidance: Generate sample records that read like a real business, in the language of the app.
```

## 6. API

```yaml id=API kind=api
operations:
  - id: API-signInSso
    name: Sign in with the company account
    method: POST
    path: /auth/sso
    response_entity: ENT-Employee
    notes: Exchanges the single sign-on result for a session. Mock account in the preview.
  - id: API-getMe
    name: Get my profile
    method: GET
    path: /me
    response_entity: ENT-Employee
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listTasks
    name: List tasks
    method: GET
    path: /tasks
    response_entity: ENT-Task
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
    notes: 'Query: status, assignee, due, page.'
  - id: API-getTask
    name: Get a task
    method: GET
    path: /tasks/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Task
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Includes its comments (ENT-TaskComment).
  - id: API-createTask
    name: Create a task
    method: POST
    path: /tasks
    request_entity: ENT-Task
    response_entity: ENT-Task
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateTask
    name: Change a task
    method: PATCH
    path: /tasks/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-Task
    response_entity: ENT-Task
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-addTaskComment
    name: Comment on a task
    method: POST
    path: /tasks/{id}/comments
    request_entity: ENT-TaskComment
    response_entity: ENT-TaskComment
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listFormTemplates
    name: List forms and checklists
    method: GET
    path: /forms
    response_entity: ENT-FormTemplate
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-getFormTemplate
    name: Get a form or checklist
    method: GET
    path: /forms/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-FormTemplate
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-submitForm
    name: Submit a form or checklist
    method: POST
    path: /submissions
    request_entity: ENT-FormSubmission
    response_entity: ENT-FormSubmission
    auth: authenticated
    notes: 'Accepted offline: queued on the phone and sent when there is signal.'
  - id: API-listSubmissions
    name: List my submissions
    method: GET
    path: /submissions
    response_entity: ENT-FormSubmission
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-createRequest
    name: Send a request
    method: POST
    path: /requests
    request_entity: ENT-ApprovalRequest
    response_entity: ENT-ApprovalRequest
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listMyRequests
    name: List my requests
    method: GET
    path: /requests
    response_entity: ENT-ApprovalRequest
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listApprovals
    name: List requests waiting for me
    method: GET
    path: /approvals
    response_entity: ENT-ApprovalRequest
    response_many: true
    auth: ROLE-manager
    roles: [ROLE-manager]
    notes: 'Query: status.'
  - id: API-getApproval
    name: Get a request to decide
    method: GET
    path: /approvals/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-ApprovalRequest
    auth: ROLE-manager
    roles: [ROLE-manager]
  - id: API-decideApproval
    name: Approve or reject
    method: POST
    path: /approvals/{id}/decision
    request_entity: ENT-ApprovalRequest
    response_entity: ENT-ApprovalRequest
    auth: ROLE-manager
    roles: [ROLE-manager]
    notes: Rejecting needs a decision note.
  - id: API-getTimesheet
    name: Get a week's timesheet
    method: GET
    path: /timesheets/current
    response_entity: ENT-Timesheet
    auth: authenticated
    notes: 'Query: week_start. Includes its entries (ENT-TimeEntry).'
  - id: API-saveTimeEntry
    name: Save a time entry
    method: PUT
    path: /timesheets/entries/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-TimeEntry
    response_entity: ENT-TimeEntry
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-submitTimesheet
    name: Submit the week
    method: POST
    path: /timesheets/{id}/submit
    response_entity: ENT-Timesheet
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listTimesheets
    name: List past timesheets
    method: GET
    path: /timesheets
    response_entity: ENT-Timesheet
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listAnnouncements
    name: List announcements
    method: GET
    path: /announcements
    response_entity: ENT-Announcement
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-getAnnouncement
    name: Get an announcement
    method: GET
    path: /announcements/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Announcement
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-acknowledgeAnnouncement
    name: Confirm I read it
    method: POST
    path: /announcements/{id}/ack
    response_entity: ENT-AnnouncementAck
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-getSyncStatus
    name: List changes waiting to sync
    method: GET
    path: /sync/status
    response_entity: ENT-SyncItem
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-syncNow
    name: Send waiting changes now
    method: POST
    path: /sync
    response_entity: ENT-SyncItem
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Sends the queued changes in order and returns any that failed or conflicted.
    source: research
  - id: API-discardPendingChange
    name: Discard a waiting change
    method: DELETE
    path: /sync/items/{id}
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
mock_guidance: A generated mock backend answers every operation; nothing leaves the device in the preview.
```

## 7. Roles

```yaml id=ROLES kind=roles
roles:
  - id: ROLE-employee
    name: Employee
    description: Does the work, fills forms and logs time.
    surface: employee
  - id: ROLE-manager
    name: Manager
    description: Everything an employee can do, plus approving requests and viewing reports for the team.
    surface: employee
```

## 8. Integrations

```yaml id=INTEGRATIONS kind=integrations
items:
  - id: INT-sso
    name: Company single sign-on
    purpose: Sign people in with their company account.
    notes: A sample company account signs in during the preview. A real identity provider (OpenID Connect
      or SAML) is configured at release.
  - id: INT-hr_system
    name: HR system
    purpose: Read people and teams and write approved leave and expenses back.
    notes: Sample people in the preview. A real HR connector is chosen at release.
  - id: INT-file_storage
    name: File storage
    purpose: Store photos and attachments from forms and checklists.
  - id: INT-company_single_sign_on
    name: Company single sign-on
    purpose: Sign-in through the company's single sign-on is the norm for employee apps.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-003
  - id: INT-send_codes_and_reminders_from_the_server
    name: Send codes and reminders from the server
    purpose: Text messages and reminders are sent through a provider API from a server, not from the app.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-006
```

## 9. Behavior

```yaml id=BEHAVIOR kind=behavior
offline: Basic cache. The last loaded lists and details stay readable without a connection, and changes
  wait on the phone until the connection returns.
deep_links: ['/announcements/[id]', '/approvals/[id]', '/checklists/[id]', '/forms/[id]', '/tasks/[id]']
notifications: [account updates]
permission_prompts:
  - Photos and files, only when the person adds an attachment
  - Exact location
  - asked only while the app is open and with a clear reason
error_conventions:
  - Show a plain-language message and a retry action, never a raw error code
  - Keep what the person typed when a request fails
  - Loading, empty, error and offline states come from the screen recipe
  - 'Never log personal data (data classification: internal)'
accessibility:
  - Every control has a text label for screen readers
  - Text meets WCAG AA contrast in light and dark mode
  - Text grows with the phone's font size setting
  - Touch targets are at least 44 by 44 points
```

## 10. Screens

### SCR-001 - /login

```yaml id=SCR-001 kind=screen
route: /login
surface: employee
recipe: login-sso
purpose: Sign in with the company account
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - sign_in_with_company: {calls: API-signInSso, go: SCR-002, on_success: save the session and open the
        home screen}
states:
  not_allowed:
    disable: sign_in_with_company
    show: Your account is not allowed to use this app. Contact your administrator
copy:
  cta: Continue with company account
  intro: Sign in with the company account
  title: Sign in
checks:
  - Signing in opens the home screen with the person's name
  - An account without access sees a plain message and no retry loop
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: sign in with the company account'
```

### SCR-002 - /home

```yaml id=SCR-002 kind=screen
route: /home
surface: employee
recipe: dashboard
purpose: Show today's tasks and shortcuts to the things the person does most
auth: authenticated
flow: FLW-001
data:
  - {bind: 'API-listTasks(mine, due)', show: [title, status, priority, due_at, location]}
sections: [greeting, sync_banner, todays_tasks, quick_actions, announcements_strip, help_hint]
actions:
  - open_task: {go: SCR-009}
  - open_tasks: {go: SCR-008}
  - open_forms: {go: SCR-011}
  - open_timesheet: {go: SCR-005}
  - open_announcements: {go: SCR-003}
  - open_my_requests: {go: SCR-019}
states:
  empty: {action: See all tasks, message: Nothing due today}
copy: {intro: Show today's tasks and shortcuts to the things the person does most, title: Today}
checks:
  - Overdue tasks are listed first and marked with text, not color alone
  - The offline banner appears when there is no signal and says how many changes are waiting
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: show today''s tasks and shortcuts to the things the person
    does most'
```

